smartinit.v4.1.0  Q1FY18 

June 2017 NAM smartinit changes to coincide with RTMA/URMA v2.6 upgrade (see docs/README for more details on changes)

* Updated GRIB2 Terrain and Land/Sea Mask files for CONUS, Hawaii, and Puerto Rico

* Converted Alaska Terrain and Land/Sea Mask files from GRIB1 to GRIB2

* Removed symbolic links from mask and topo files

* Removed creation of all GRIB1 files, conus (5km), alaska (6 km) and ak_rtmages (6 km) files.

* New datacards will be delivered prior to the 30-day parallel if they are approved by the SREC committee for this 
  implementation

#===============================================================================
 IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS 
#===============================================================================
1.  svn checkout https://svnemc.ncep.noaa.gov/projects/smartinit/tags/RB-v4.1.0 smartinit.v4.1.0

    to set up and run on WCOSS phase 2.

2.  Build sorc codes smartinit_g2.fd, smartprecip_g2.fd
       
	The modulefile used for the build is in modulefiles/SMARTINIT/v4.1.0.  Copy it to a location from which it can
	be loaded (/nwprod2/modulefiles/SMARTINIT or something similar). 

	In the smartinit sorc directory "smartinit.v4.1.0/sorc" type
		./build_smartinit.scr
	to compile the codes sequentially.  All executables will be copied over to the smartinit "exec" directory.

4.  Use ...docs/smartinit.ver file if desired to set
      model_ver=v4.1.0  parameter

5.  I recommend you remove the following directories, as they are no longer needed or used:

	ecf/sminit_ak
	ecf/sminit_conus
	ecf/sminit_dgex-ak
	ecf/sminit_dgex-cs 

    The CONUS (5km), Alaska (6km) and ak_rtmages (6 km) and DGEX smartinits are no longer needed or used.

6.  Job Dependencies: 
     Upstream: NAM/NAM Nest, SREF; 
     Upstream links:

     NAM/NAM Nest 
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.bgrd3d${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.priconest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.hawaiinest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.conusnest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.alaskanest.bsmart${hh}.tm00

     SREF
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb212.prob_3hrly
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb243.prob_3hrly
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb216.prob_3hrly

     Downstream: RTMA, URMA
     Downstream links(J-Jobs that use NAM smartinit files): 

     /nwprod2/rtma.v2.5.0/jobs/JRTMA_GETGUESS
     /nwprod2/urma.v2.5.0/jobs/JURMA_GETGUESS

7.  Test plan: 

	Test J-Jobs jobs/JNAM_SMINIT for a full 24-hour period.

8.  Technical Details:
	Runtime: ~3 hours, 30 minutes wallclock
	Nodes: 12
	Tasks per node: 12
	Consumable memory: 4916 mb
	Serial vs parallel: Parallel (wgrib2 only)
	Disk Storage: Has decreased by 21.4 GB total (removed all GRIB1, conus (5km), alaska (6km), and ak_rtmages (6km) files)

7.  New output files: None

8.  Flow Diagram:

    https://drive.google.com/a/noaa.gov/file/d/0B7IqRnJWIYHlaVhCcUdaQ1RaZzQ/view?usp=sharing

NOTE: Details on all changes to nam smartinit are found at docs/README - Search for 4.1.0 for changes related to this implemenation.

